	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42269</id><title>When Protection Meets the Sea: Rethinking Marine Protected Areas with Fishing Communities</title><updated>2026-02-05T10:03:48-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42269" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Whale-Shark_Kerala-Graffiti.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Whale-Shark_Kerala-Graffiti.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
DELHI, February 5 (IPS)  - Melanie Brown has been fishing salmon in Bristol Bay, Alaska, for more than 30 years. An Indigenous fisherwoman and a coordinating committee member of the World Forum of Fisher Peoples, she speaks about the sea with deep care and lived knowledge.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42269&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “When Protection Meets the Sea: Rethinking Marine Protected Areas with Fishing Communities”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/Whale-Shark_Kerala-Graffiti-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42268</id><title>To Fix the Rupture, Trade is not Enough</title><updated>2026-02-05T08:58:28-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42268" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/UNRIC-Miranda-Alexander.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/UNRIC-Miranda-Alexander.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
KATHMANDU, Nepal, February 5 (IPS)  - Will trade be enough to navigate the current waves of chaos and disorder that are underpinning the ongoing rifts among competing powerful and hegemon nations and the rest?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42268&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “To Fix the Rupture, Trade is not Enough”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/02/UNRIC-Miranda-Alexander-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42278</id><title>UN Police ‘indispensable’ to fulfilling peacekeeping mandates, Security Council hears</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42278" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-10-2025-UNMISS-South-Sudan-her-lens.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-10-2025-UNMISS-South-Sudan-her-lens.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The head of UN Peacekeeping on Thursday called for greater support for international police officers deployed to field missions at a time when financial resources are dwindling and multilateralism is waning. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42278&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN Police ‘indispensable’ to fulfilling peacekeeping mandates, Security Council hears”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-10-2025-UNMISS-South-Sudan-her-lens.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42277</id><title>Chad: Africa’s refugee haven struggles with its own stark challenges</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42277" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/24-06-2025-UNHCR-Sudan.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/24-06-2025-UNHCR-Sudan.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Amid the ongoing war in Sudan, Chad, the country receiving the most refugees in Central Africa, saw slight improvements in its humanitarian situation last year, but as one of the most vulnerable nations on the African continent, it is still struggling to support four million people in need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42277&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Chad: Africa’s refugee haven struggles with its own stark challenges”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/24-06-2025-UNHCR-Sudan.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42276</id><title>World News in Brief: UN condemns attack on civilians in Nigeria, updates from Gaza and West Bank, relief flights to resume in Yemen</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42276" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2019/01/2019-01-18-NIG-Borno-Rann-AerialView-NIR_20180706_4617.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2019/01/2019-01-18-NIG-Borno-Rann-AerialView-NIR_20180706_4617.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN Secretary-General on Thursday strongly condemned a deadly terrorist attack in Kwara state in western Nigeria, where more than 100 people were reportedly killed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42276&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “World News in Brief: UN condemns attack on civilians in Nigeria, updates from Gaza and West Bank, relief flights to resume in Yemen”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2019/01/2019-01-18-NIG-Borno-Rann-AerialView-NIR_20180706_4617.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42275</id><title>Fatwas, faith and fallacies: Myth-busting female genital mutilation in Africa</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42275" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/05-02-2026-UNFPA-Djibouti.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/05-02-2026-UNFPA-Djibouti.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Olivia Albert, 19, was subjected to female genital (FGM) mutilation when she was 14. She told the UN sexual and reproductive health agency (UNFPA) that she hid her pain because everyone around her said it was normal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42275&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Fatwas, faith and fallacies: Myth-busting female genital mutilation in Africa”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/05-02-2026-UNFPA-Djibouti.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42274</id><title>M23 rebels: UN sees progress in talks but warns violence persists</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42274" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/20-01-2026-UNV-MONUSCO.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/20-01-2026-UNV-MONUSCO.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The United Nations has welcomed signs of progress in talks aimed at reducing violence in eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42274&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “M23 rebels: UN sees progress in talks but warns violence persists”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/20-01-2026-UNV-MONUSCO.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42273</id><title>Child malnutrition hits catastrophic levels in parts of Sudan</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42273" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/26-02-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/26-02-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acute malnutrition among children has reached catastrophic levels in parts of Sudan’s North Darfur and Greater Kordofan, UN-backed analysts warned on Thursday, as conflict, mass displacement and denials of aid push the country deeper into a famine-risk emergency.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42273&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Child malnutrition hits catastrophic levels in parts of Sudan”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/26-02-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42272</id><title>UN lauds $6 billion US funding approval towards ending HIV/AIDS</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42272" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2025-UNAIDS-Zimbabwe-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2025-UNAIDS-Zimbabwe-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN agency leading the global effort to end HIV/AIDS worldwide welcomed legislative approval from the United States on Thursday for a $6 billion spending package to help tackle the disease, following nearly a year of sharp aid cuts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42272&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN lauds $6 billion US funding approval towards ending HIV/AIDS”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/28-02-2025-UNAIDS-Zimbabwe-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42271</id><title>Cuba: UN warns of possible humanitarian ‘collapse’, as oil supplies dwindle</title><updated>2026-02-05T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42271" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/21-01-2026-UN-Cuba-05.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/21-01-2026-UN-Cuba-05.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN on Wednesday warned of potential humanitarian “collapse” in Cuba, following Washington’s attempt to block oil supplies from reaching the island.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/02/05/42271&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Cuba: UN warns of possible humanitarian ‘collapse’, as oil supplies dwindle”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/21-01-2026-UN-Cuba-05.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry></feed><!-- 0.0015s -->